From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:45:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: wait for the BCM4398's boot interrupt

The BCM4398's firmware writes an interim address to the last word of
RAM before its shared area's, and signals the end of its boot with a
mailbox interrupt, which Broadcom's driver waits for before it reads
the address (dhdpcie_wait_readshared_area_addr(), "recd. boot intr").
brcmfmac took the interim address and failed the firmware's API checks.

Interrupts are not set up yet at that point, so poll the PCIe core's
mailbox status through BAR0's fixed window onto it, then read the
address.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c        | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index d56650a34..e63d9a8f2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2423,6 +2423,37 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Wait for FW init\n");
 	sharedram_addr = sharedram_addr_written;
 	loop_counter = BRCMF_PCIE_FW_UP_TIMEOUT / 50;
+	/*
+	 * The BCM4398's firmware writes an interim address to the last word
+	 * of RAM before the real one, and signals the end of its boot with a
+	 * mailbox interrupt, which Google's driver waits for (dhd_pcie.c
+	 * dhdpcie_wait_readshared_area_addr(), "boot intr"). Interrupts are
+	 * not set up yet, so poll for it.
+	 */
+	if (devinfo->pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4398_DEVICE_ID) {
+		u32 mbint = BRCMF_PCIE_BARO_PCIE_ENUM_OFFSET +
+			    devinfo->reginfo->mailboxint;
+		u32 intstatus = 0;
+
+		brcmf_pcie_select_core(devinfo, BCMA_CORE_PCIE2);
+		while (loop_counter) {
+			intstatus = brcmf_pcie_read_reg32(devinfo, mbint);
+			if (intstatus && intstatus != 0xffffffff)
+				break;
+			msleep(50);
+			loop_counter--;
+		}
+		brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "boot interrupt %#x after %u ms\n", intstatus,
+			  (BRCMF_PCIE_FW_UP_TIMEOUT / 50 - loop_counter) * 50);
+		if (intstatus && intstatus != 0xffffffff)
+			brcmf_pcie_write_reg32(devinfo,
+					       BRCMF_PCIE_BARO_PCIE_ENUM_OFFSET +
+					       devinfo->reginfo->mailboxint,
+					       intstatus);
+		sharedram_addr = brcmf_pcie_read_ram32(devinfo,
+						       devinfo->ci->ramsize -
+						       4);
+	}
 	while ((sharedram_addr == sharedram_addr_written) && (loop_counter)) {
 		msleep(50);
 		sharedram_addr = brcmf_pcie_read_ram32(devinfo,
